WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.509
Here's something very interesting and gross
I want to be clear.

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:11.190
But we're looking at it from from a perspective
of electoral politics, the Trump 2020 campaign

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:17.480
and the 2020 Republican platform in the last
three days have confirmed and gone back to

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.060
being more anti-gay and more anti trans.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.869
Now, the reason this is interesting is that
Donald Trump never ran as your traditional

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:29.779
socially conservative, anti-gay Republican.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:37.400
He very decidedly focused during his campaign
in 2015 and 2016 on really an economic populist

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.039
message is right wing populism.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.440
But it's an economic populist message.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.590
I'll fix trade because trade and these trade
deals, NAFTA, China, the they're screwing

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.100
the average person.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.239
I'm going to protect our borders and therefore
protect jobs for average people.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:56.390
That type of language was Trump's focus in
2016.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:02.510
And we showed we saw the effect of that during
the Republican primary of 2016, where the

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.880
evangelical and the Christian support was
more around other candidates.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.360
Ted Cruz is an example.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.630
I forget who else had early Christian support.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:16.030
Now, eventually, the Christians came around
and mostly voted for Donald Trump because,

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.790
number one, they certainly weren't going to
vote for Hillary Clinton.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.420
Number two, Trump started kowtowing to them
a little bit.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.950
He told this completely unbelievable story
about how, despite being pro-choice his entire

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.750
life, he essentially met a kid.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.700
He, like the friend of his, had a kid that
he liked and the person had thought about

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.869
getting an abortion and that made Trump see
the light and have an awakening where he was

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:37.149
now against abortion.

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:38.340
Totally unbelievable.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.450
But he he played to it, said the Bible is
his favorite book up there with Art of the

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.450
Deal.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.670
So eventually the Christians came over to
him.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.710
But the anti-gay message was not a big part
of Donald Trump's campaign.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:56.630
The anti-gay rhetoric for Republicans has
historically been a really great way to raise

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.789
money, even if the anti-gay crowd is not as
big as it once was.

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:06.240
They will still donate if they believe that
you're with them on so-called family values,

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.520
which typically include being anti gay.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:15.050
So Donald Trump and the Republican Party seem
so desperate right now to stop the damage

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:20.040
that is being done by Trump's presidency to
the Republican Party, that they are bringing

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.450
back an anti-gay focus and it's because they're
desperate.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.590
So Trump sees the numbers.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.030
Women are going to Biden in record numbers.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.569
Young people are sticking with Biden.

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:32.849
Older folks are going with Biden.

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:38.909
And the idea is, let's get back to the anti-gay
focus of five or 10 years ago and try to pull

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:42.379
in some people, particularly people who will
donate a lot of money.

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:48.239
So on Friday, the Trump administration rolled
back an Obama era transgender health care

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:49.239
protection.

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:50.540
That's part of Obamacare.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:56.519
And what they're doing is returning to the
government's interpretation of sex discrimination,

00:02:56.519 --> 00:03:01.450
according to what they call the plain meaning
of sex as male or female, determined by biology.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:08.879
So this essentially dismisses any concept
of treating trans people in accordance with

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:15.239
their sexual identity and all of the protections
associated with that would go away.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:21.400
The Republican National Committee has also
now called for just leaving their 2016 platform

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.459
unchanged and making it their 2020 platform.

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:28.750
That is a platform that called for banning
same sex marriage.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:35.050
Now the timing, remember June 2015, the Supreme
Court said states can't ban same sex marriage

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:36.050
anymore.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.239
So it de facto made same sex marriage legal
nationally.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:40.560
That was June 2015.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.129
The Republican primary was already starting
to get going then.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:51.180
And the Republican platform contained opposition
to same sex marriage at that time, despite

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.930
what the Supreme Court said now, over the
last four years, as you probably know, even

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.490
among Republicans.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:01.400
Public opinion has been moved more and more
into same sex marriage is OK.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.550
This is not something we really want to fight
about anymore.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:09.720
And the anti-gay activism has focused more
around religious freedom, not baking cakes,

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.890
that sort of thing.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:16.180
But Republicans have decided they're going
to keep that as part of their 2020 platform

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.160
ban same sex marriage.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.710
So understand, this is not an oversight.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:27.960
This is part of continuing to counteract the
unpopularity of Donald Trump and the fact

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.650
that this is also dragging down a bunch of
different Senate candidates.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:32.650
Joni Ernst.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.790
Now we saw is doing poorly.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.180
We're going to talk about that.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.720
So they're going back to their old faithful
methods of bringing in bigots and raising

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.720
money.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:47.330
So the same platform that they are reinstating
supports can so-called conversion therapy

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.570
for LGBT individuals.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:53.490
The idea that typically religious type services
that they call their therapy, I don't call

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:58.240
it therapy, can convert your sexual orientation
or gender identity.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.520
They want to continue supporting the rights
of businesses to discriminate against people

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:08.270
on the basis of their sexual orientation or
gender identity, which remember in some states

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.370
is already illegal by state law.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.620
In other states, it is very much legal.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.230
Now, there is some other stuff thrown in there
as well.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:22.540
So in total, what we are seeing, you know,
Trump's 2016 campaign was an outlier in terms

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.930
of Republican campaigns.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.070
There is no doubt.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:30.780
But now in the face of polls that look really
bad for Donald Trump, they are going back

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.160
to the old faithful tactics of Republican
candidates.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.320
Do the anti-gay stuff again pander to racists?

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.840
We're seeing examples of that lately.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.980
Pander to xenophobes.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:41.980
They're doing it all.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.750
This is the strategy.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:49.520
Pander to the worst of the worst hope that
the economy bounces back just enough between

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:54.200
now and November that you can justify, hey,
vote to reelect me.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:00.100
And the third part of this sort of hydra is
suppress enough of the vote.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:04.990
That along with pandering to the racists and
the homophobes and a slight improvement in

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.340
the economy.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.300
You can get enough votes to get yourself reelected.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:15.270
Now, remember, if we go out and vote in overwhelming
numbers, this won't work.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.691
If we don't go out and vote in overwhelming
numbers, it actually may get Donald Trump

00:06:19.691 --> 00:06:21.100
reelected.

